@props(title: text)
<article class="mx-auto min-h-[70vh] max-w-4xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-20"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500" href="/">← Back to home</a><span class="mt-10 block text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-600">About the starter</span><h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">A simple place to start.</h1><p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">This is an Axon Web starter styled with Tailwind CSS. Use it as the starting point for a site, dashboard, or small web application.</p><div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3"><section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5"><h2 class="font-semibold">Native server rendering</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Templates compile to Axon functions. Pages arrive as complete HTML.</p></section><section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5"><h2 class="font-semibold">Standard Tailwind</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Default colors, spacing, typography utilities, and responsive breakpoints. Edit the classes to make it yours.</p></section><section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5"><h2 class="font-semibold">Optional JavaScript</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">The counter and filter load small browser modules. This about page ships without JavaScript.</p></section></div><div class="mt-10 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 p-5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">The framework is an early prototype with GET routes, typed templates, client navigation, and static export. It does not yet offer the full feature set of Astro or Next.js.</div></article>
